<h1><span lang="EN-US" style="mso-ansi-language:EN-US;">System Set-up</span><span lang="EN-US" style="mso-ansi-language:EN-US;">&#160;</span></h1>
<hr align="center" size="5" class="whs3">
<p class="stepstitle">Localiser set-up</p>
<p>In the next section of the KUBE help TOC, you can find information about setting up your localiser. Generally speaking, setting up the localiser is a three steps process:</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Localiser Configuration</b></span>: When the hardware assembly is complete the next step is to start a specific utility software to configure the localiser.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Localiser Probe Calibration</b></span>: Calibrating a localiser is needed to maintain a high degree of accuracy.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Localiser Performance Check</b></span>: <span lang="EN-GB">This section describes how to check if the localiser performance is within specification.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="stepstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Alignment</span></p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Process</b></span>: Alignment is the process of registering the sensor co-ordinate system to the localiser co-ordinate system. Without an accurate alignment, the data produced by the ModelMaker system will be out of specification.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Alignment Check</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span> This section describes three methods of checking accuracy and repeatability of the ModelMaker system.</p>
</li>
</ul>
